# Enhanced xv6-RISC-V Operating System

**Developed by: Wirsha**

## Overview
An enhanced xv6-RISC-V teaching operating system with additional scheduling, process management, system calls, and performance statistics.

## Implemented Features
1. Priority Scheduling
2. Lottery Scheduling
3. CPU Tick Tracking
4. Process Information
5. Memory Statistics
6. System Call Counter
7. Sleep/Wakeup Statistics
8. Process Tree
9. Disk Sync
10. Advanced Sleep/Wakeup

## Requirements
- RISC-V GNU Toolchain
- QEMU for RISC-V
- Ubuntu or WSL Ubuntu

## Build and Run
Run these commands:
- make clean
- make
- make qemu

## Testing
The project builds successfully and has been tested in QEMU. Individual tests were performed for scheduling, process information, memory statistics, system call counting, and sleep/wakeup behavior.

## Original Project Credits
Based on the xv6-RISC-V educational operating system developed at MIT.
Original repository: https://github.com/mit-pdos/xv6-riscv
